# Browser QA (MananChintan)

Use **Cursor Browser** (`cursor-ide-browser` MCP), not Playwright, for interactive QA. Google OAuth blocks Playwright/Chromium automation.

## Prerequisites

1. `npm run dev` running → `http://localhost:3000`
2. **Cursor Settings → Features → Browser** enabled (built-in; no `mcp.json` entry required)
3. Sign in once in the Browser pane with **Continue with Google** (allowlisted account). Session cookies persist per workspace.

## MCP workflow

1. `browser_tabs` list — reuse an open tab when possible
2. `browser_navigate` → target URL
3. `browser_lock` → interact → `browser_unlock` when done
4. `browser_snapshot` before every click/type; short waits + re-snapshot instead of one long sleep
5. After bottom-nav taps, active tab should highlight immediately; main area shows a **route skeleton** until content loads (no full-screen splash)

## Smoke checklist (report pass/fail + screenshot on failure)

| Step | Action | Pass criteria |
|------|--------|----------------|
| Auth | Open `/home` | App shell (header + nav), not Google CTA |
| Nav | Tap Home, Feed, Standings, Swadhyay, Smruti | URL changes; active tab highlighted |
| Profile | Header avatar → sheet | "Profile" title; Calendar link; close works |
| Smruti | `/smruti` → add photo → caption → Post | Lands on `/feed`; post visible |
| Feed | `/feed` scroll | Main scrolls; posts load |

## URLs

- Local: `http://localhost:3000`
- Production preview: team Vercel URL (sign in separately)

## When blocked

- **Google “browser not secure”** → use Cursor Browser (this), not `playwright codegen`
- **Not signed in** → user completes Google login in Browser pane, then re-run checklist
